{"id":"word:hebrew:H7819","type":"word","title":"שָׁחַט","subtitle":"H7819 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to slaughter (in sacrifice or massacre)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to שָׁחַט (H7819) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 82 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"שָׁחַט (shâchaṭ) means to slaughter (in sacrifice or massacre) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 18 40."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"שָׁחַט","transliteration":"shâchaṭ","pronunciation":"shaw-khat'","strong":"H7819","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7819","partOfSpeech":"v n-f","forms":["וְ/שָׁחַ֣ט","וַֽ/יִּשְׁחֲט֖וּ","וַֽ/יִּשְׁחֲטוּ֙","וַ/יִּשְׁחֲט֣וּ","וְ/שָׁחַ֥ט"],"morphs":[["HC/Vqq3ms",16],["HC/Vqw3mp",12],["HC/Vqw3ms",8],["HVqi3ms",6],["HVqi3mp",5],["HC/Vqw3ms/Sp3mp",3],["HC/Vqq2ms",3],["HC/Vqw3mp/Sp3mp",2],["HC/Vqv2mp",2],["HR/Vqc",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to slaughter (in sacrifice or massacre)","usage":"kill, offer, shoot out, slay, slaughter.","full":"H7819. shachat שָׁחַט verb slaughter, beat (originally beat, flay ? compare Assyrian ša—â‰u , flay , take off dress; Arabic slay (but = — ; is this loan-word in Arabic ?); Late Hebrew = Biblical Hebrew, especially in ritual); — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular ׳שׁ Jer 39:6 +, suffix וּשְׁחָטוֺ consecutive Lev 3:2 , etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִשְׁחַט 4:24 +, 2 feminine singular וַתִּשְׁחֲטִי Ezek 16:21 , 3 masculine plural suffix וַיִּשְׁחָט֫וּהוּ Judg 12:6 ; Imperative masculine plural שַׁחֲטוּ Exod 12:21 ; 2Chr 35:6 ; Infinitive absolute שָׁחֹט Isa 22:13 ; construct לִשְׁחֹט Gen 22:10 , וֺט - Ezek 40:39 , suffix שַׁחֲטָם (Ges § 64a ) 23:39 ; Participle active שׁוֺחֵט Isa 66:3 , etc.; passive שָׁחוּט 1Kin 10:16 +, etc.; — slaughter: 1 beast for food 1Sam 14:32 , 34 (twice in verse); Isa 22:13 (|| הָרַג ), compare Lev 17:3 (twice in verse), for blood Gen 37:31 (E). 2 usually (51 t.; Hexateuch only P, 38 t.) technical term of killing sacrifice (BJacob ZAW xvii (1897), 5i ), 1Sam 1:25 ; Exod 29:11 ; Lev 1:5 , 11 ; 4:24 ; 9:8 ; Num 19:3 ; 2Chr 29:22 (twice in verse); 29:24 +; absolute Ezek 40:41 ( אֶל location); bird Lev 14:5-6 , 50 , 51 ; beast in illicit sacrifice Isa 66:3 ; with accusative of sacrifice ( חַטָאת אָשָׁם, עוֺלָה, , etc.) Ezek 40:39 ( אֶל location), 40:42 ; 44:11 ; Lev 4:24 ; 7:2 ; 14:13 +; passover lamb Exod 12:6 , accusative הַמֶּסַח 12:21 ; 2Chr 30:15 ; 35:1 , 6 , 11 ; Ezra 6:20 . 3 slaughter person Judg 12:6 ; 1Kin 18:40 ; 2Kin 10:7 , 14 ( אֶל location), 25:7 = Jer 39:6 a = 52:10 a, 39:6 b = 52:10 b, 41:7; ׳י subject Num 14:16 (JE); in human sacrifice Gen 22:10 (E), to false gods Ezek 16:21 ; 23:39 ; Isa 57:5 . 4 passive participle = beaten, hammered , שָׁחוּט זָהָב 1Kin 10:16-17 , 2Chr 9:15 a 9:16 , of shekels 9:15 ; so also Jer 9:7 Qr חֵץשָׁחוּט (&gt; Kt שׁוֺחֵט ) hammered (i.e. sharpened) arrow . Niph`al Imperfect 3masculine singular יִשָּׁחֵט Num 11:22 (J) be slaughtered for food (subject beast); 3 feminine singular תִּשָּׁחֵט Lev 6:18 (twice in verse) (P) be slain , of sacrifice. שְׁחֲטָה noun feminine ( Qal Infinitive construct Kö i. 263 ) doubtful word; — ׳וְשׁ הֶעְמִיקוּ שֵׂטִים Hosea 5:2 RV (compare AV) the revolters are gone deep in slaughtering ['Opferschlächterei' Kö ii. 1. 590, n. 1 ], Ew Now (formerly), Che in corrupting (read then שַׁחֲתָה ); We Now GASm Marti הַשִּׁטִּים שַׁחַת have made deep the pit of Shittim (as place of idolatry). שְׁחִין see שׁחן . שְׁחִיף see [ שָׂחִיף ]. below, שָׁחִיס Isa 37:30 = סָחִישׁ (in || 2Kin 19:29 ), q. v. שׁחל (√ of following; Dl Prol.34 compare Assyrian ša—âlu , call, proclaim ; perhaps both onomatopoetic, as Arabic bray (of ass), compare Nö ZMG xi (1886), 725 ).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 18 40","keyReferences":["1Kgs 18 40","1Sam 1 25","1Sam 14 32","1Sam 14 34","1Sam 14 34","2Chr 29 22","2Chr 29 2